  "summary": {
    "en": "Ambazonian separatists have shot a journalist in Bamenda and a young girl was killed in the same area, indicating continued attacks on civilians. Boko Haram is rebuilding its ranks, training about 8,000 children and preparing a new generation of fighters, while Cameroon urges drones and joint border patrols to secure the Nigeria-Cameroon frontier. The government has offered the Zina and Makary oil blocks to investors twelve years after exploration was halted, signalling an economic outreach amid the conflict. The conflict caused 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
